// .mcp.json.example
//
// .mcp.json is currently an empty stub: { "mcpServers": {} }
//
// This file documents *intent*, not a working config — no server entries
// have been decided on yet. Do not copy anything below into .mcp.json
// without confirming the server is actually wanted first.
//
// Candidates that may be added here once decided:
//   - "github"   → GitHub MCP server, for issue/PR-aware workflows once
//                  this repo has a GitHub remote and it's worth wiring up.
//   - a Foundry/on-chain MCP server, if one proves useful once
//     contracts/ exists.
//
// Shape each entry would take (illustrative only — not a real config):
// {
//   "mcpServers": {
//     "github": {
//       "command": "npx",
//       "args": ["-y", "@modelcontextprotocol/server-github"],
//       "env": {
//         "GITHUB_PERSONAL_ACCESS_TOKEN": "${GITHUB_TOKEN}"
//       }
//     }
//   }
// }
//
// Note: env values must always be references like ${VAR_NAME}, resolved
// from the environment — never a literal token. See
// .claude/rules/security.md, rule (a).
